work_item_steps
  issue 1133
  purpose "The shell steps and file templates a repository work item ends with, as data. Hive Mind's three 2026-09-13 runs left their result in the working tree: nothing read the issue when only a remote connector could fetch, nothing committed, nothing pushed, and the workflow the issue asked for was never written. The steps that close those gaps are wording, and wording lives here rather than in Rust (VISION.md, section: Code As A Meta Language)."
  filled_by "src/agentic_coding/work_item_steps.rs"
  placeholders "{kind} issue or pr, from the work item's URL. {target} the work item's URL. {subject} the shell-quoted commit subject. {body} the shell-quoted commit body. {branch} the branch the request named, or HEAD. {path} the artifact the recipe writes. {count} how many files a commit request lists. {paths} those files, comma-separated. {reference} the issue or pull-request URL the work resolves. {command} one verification command of the recipe."
  note "The reads are two calls rather than one --jq expression because a quoted scalar here cannot carry both quote characters a jq string would need. Since issue #1155 every read also prints its own exit status as a sentinel line, so a client that drops the status field cannot make a failed read look successful. The curl read asks GitHub for the raw body, which is why it is a single call."
  issue_view_command "gh {kind} view {target} --json title --jq .title && echo && gh {kind} view {target} --json body --jq .body; printf '\n__formal_ai_exit=%s\n' $?"
  issue_fetch_prompt "Return only the work-item title and body from the fetched page as faithful source text; for a pull request, the body is its description. Preserve requirements, paths, code spans and line breaks. Do not solve, summarize, rewrite or execute the work item."
  issue_rest_read_command "curl -fsSL -H 'Accept: application/vnd.github.raw+json' https://api.github.com/repos/{owner}/{repo}/{kind}/{number}; printf '\n__formal_ai_exit=%s\n' $?"
  issue_api_read_command "gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/{kind}/{number} --jq .title && echo && gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/{kind}/{number} --jq .body; printf '\n__formal_ai_exit=%s\n' $?"
  page-note "Issue #1560: a fetched work-item page is a document around the work item. These markers find its title and body; the rest is site chrome and is dropped. A page that matches the title suffix or a chrome line but has no body start is rejected, so the REST and gh api reads of issue #1155 run instead. Alternatives are separated by |."
  page-title-suffix " · GitHub"
  page-title-separator " · "
  page-chrome-lines "Skip to content|Dismiss alert|{{ message }}"
  page-body-start "Issue body actions"
  page-body-end "ActivitySign up for free to join this conversation on GitHub|Sign up for free to join this conversation on GitHub"
  page-body-end-lines "Footer|You can’t perform that action at this time."
  read_failed_report "The work item at {target} could not be read, so nothing was planned for it and no plan record was written. Reads tried this session, each with its result:\n{attempts}"
  commit_command 'git add -A && git commit -q -m {subject} -m {body} && if test -n "$(git remote)"; then __formal_ai_push_ref={branch} && if test -n "$(git symbolic-ref --quiet --short HEAD)"; then if test "$__formal_ai_push_ref" = HEAD; then __formal_ai_push_ref=$(git branch --show-current); fi; else exit 1; fi && test -n "$__formal_ai_push_ref" && git push -q origin "$__formal_ai_push_ref"; fi && git rev-parse HEAD'
  commit_command_without_body 'git add -A && git commit -q -m {subject} && if test -n "$(git remote)"; then __formal_ai_push_ref={branch} && if test -n "$(git symbolic-ref --quiet --short HEAD)"; then if test "$__formal_ai_push_ref" = HEAD; then __formal_ai_push_ref=$(git branch --show-current); fi; else exit 1; fi && test -n "$__formal_ai_push_ref" && git push -q origin "$__formal_ai_push_ref"; fi && git rev-parse HEAD'
  recipe_commit_command 'git add -- {files} && (if git diff --cached --quiet -- {files}; then echo __formal_ai_commit_unchanged; else git commit --only -q -m {subject} -m {body} -- {files}; fi) && __formal_ai_push_ref={branch} && if test -n "$(git symbolic-ref --quiet --short HEAD)"; then if test "$__formal_ai_push_ref" = HEAD; then __formal_ai_push_ref=$(git branch --show-current); fi; else exit 1; fi && test -n "$__formal_ai_push_ref" && git push -q origin "$__formal_ai_push_ref" && git rev-parse HEAD'
  subject_added "feat: add {path}"
  subject_updated "fix: update {path}"
  subject_many "chore: update {count} files ({paths})"
  subject_none "chore: commit pending changes"
  body_resolves "Resolves {reference}"
  workflow_path ".github/workflows/run.yml"
  workflow_template "# Runs {path} on every push and pull request with the commands the\n# change was verified with.\nname: Run {path}\n\non:\n  push:\n  pull_request:\n\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n\njobs:\n  run:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    timeout-minutes: 15\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@{checkout_ref} # {checkout_tag}\n"
  workflow_command_step "      - run: |\n          {command}\n"
  stuck_step_report "This session already completed the step below, and repeating it would not change anything, so the step and its last result are reported instead.\nStep: {step}\nLast result:\n{result}"

  commit_nothing_marker "__formal_ai_commit_unchanged"
  workflow_path_named ".github/workflows/{name}.yml"
  pr_comments_command "gh pr view {target} --json comments,reviews --jq {filter}"
  pr_edit_command 'pr_body={body} && if test "$(gh pr view {target} --json body --jq .body)" != "$pr_body"; then gh pr edit {target} --body "$pr_body"; fi'
  pr_edit_titled_command 'pr_title=$(gh issue view {issue} --json title --jq .title) && test -n "$pr_title" && pr_body={body} && if test "$(gh pr view {target} --json title --jq .title)" != "$pr_title" || test "$(gh pr view {target} --json body --jq .body)" != "$pr_body"; then gh pr edit {target} --title "$pr_title" --body "$pr_body"; fi'
  pr_ready_command 'test -z "$(git status --porcelain)" && pr_draft=$(gh pr view {target} --json isDraft --jq .isDraft) && if test "$pr_draft" = true; then gh pr ready {target}; fi'
  pr_body_template "Verified artifact: {path}\n\nVerification commands:\n{commands}\n\nResolves {reference}"
  pr_feedback_review_report "Pull request feedback requires review before readiness:\n{output}"
  prepared_work_pr_body "Updated prepared work on `{branch}`.\n\nChanged files:\n{paths}\n\nGit diff whitespace validation completed.\n\nResolves {reference}"
  prepared_work_feedback_report "Pull request feedback needs source review before this prepared work can be marked ready:\n{output}"
  prepared_work_stopped_report "Prepared-work continuation stopped at `{command}`:\n{output}"
  prepared_work_ready_report "Committed the prepared changes, pushed `{branch}`, updated {reference}, and marked the pull request ready. Review feedback was retrieved; source changes still require review against that feedback."
  read_attempt_run_line "- `{command}` — {outcome}"
  read_attempt_run_reason_line "- `{command}` — {reason} (answered: {outcome})"
  read_attempt_fetch_line "- fetch {url} — {outcome}"
  read_failure_exit_status "exit status {status}"
  prerequisite_grant_required_report "Missing prerequisite `{program}`. Workspace installation requires FORMAL_AI_INSTALL_GRANT=workspace. Failed command: `{command}`\n{output}"
  prerequisite_no_recipe_report "Publisher `{url}` provided no typed, verifiable setup recipe for `{program}`; installation was not planned."
  prerequisite_grant_exceeded_report "The publisher setup recipe exceeds the workspace installation grant."
  prerequisite_path_prefix 'PATH={bins}:"$PATH"; export PATH'
  prerequisite_retry_command "{prefix} && {steps} &&\n# __formal_ai_prerequisite_retry\n{command}"
  plan-event-append-command 'mkdir -p -- .formal-ai && (lock={lock_path}; tries=0; until (set -C; : > "$lock") 2>/dev/null; do tries=$((tries + 1)); [ "$tries" -lt 40 ] || exit 75; sleep 0.025; done; cleanup(){ rm -f -- "$lock"; }; trap cleanup EXIT; if [ -f {path} ]; then grep -Fqx -- {identity} {path}; status=$?; [ "$status" -le 1 ] || exit "$status"; else status=1; fi; if [ "$status" -eq 1 ]; then printf "\n%s" {event} >> {path} || exit $?; fi; awk -v identity={identity} "\$0==\"general_change_plan\" {if(record)exit; header=\$0; next} \$0==identity {record=1; print header} record && NF {print}" {path})'
  agent-file-read-frame "<file>\n{body}\n\n(End of file - total {lines} lines)\n</file>"
  plan-event-shell-aliases "bash exec_command shell run_shell_command"
  filesystem-collection-setup 'formal_ai_destination={destination}; if test -d "$formal_ai_destination" || [ "${formal_ai_destination%/}" != "$formal_ai_destination" ]; then formal_ai_leaf="${formal_ai_source%/}"; formal_ai_destination="${formal_ai_destination%/}/${formal_ai_leaf##*/}"; fi; formal_ai_parent="${formal_ai_destination%/*}"; if [ "$formal_ai_parent" = "$formal_ai_destination" ]; then formal_ai_parent=.; fi; '
  filesystem-collection-check 'for formal_ai_source in {sources}; do {setup}{check} || exit $?; done'
  command-capture-setup 'formal_ai_capture_target={target}; formal_ai_capture_parent=${formal_ai_capture_target%/*}; if [ "$formal_ai_capture_parent" != "$formal_ai_capture_target" ]; then mkdir -p -- "$formal_ai_capture_parent" || exit $?; fi; ( '
  command-capture-end ' ) > "$formal_ai_capture_target"'
  command-capture-readback "cat {target}"

  branch-binding-patterns '["^(?:Keep|Maintain) (?:the )?(?:solution|changes|work|result) (?:on|in) (?:the )?branch (.+)$","^(?:Work|Commit|Push) (?:on|to) (?:the )?branch (.+)$","^Use (?:the )?branch (.+)$","^Держи решение в ветке (.+)$","^समाधान को शाखा (.+) पर रखें[।.]?$","^将解决方案保留在分支 (.+) 上[。.]?$","^Mantén la solución en la rama (.+)$","^Your prepared branch: (.+)$"]'
  workflow-binding-patterns '["^(?:Save|Write|Create|Place|Put) (?:the |a )?(?:GitHub Actions )?workflow (?:as|at|to|in) ([^ ]+)","^Use ([^ ]+) (?:as|for) (?:the )?(?:GitHub Actions )?workflow","^保存工作流(?:到|为) ([^ ]+)","^Сохрани (?:workflow|рабочий процесс) (?:в|как) ([^ ]+)","^Guarda (?:el )?workflow (?:en|como) ([^ ]+)"]'
  target_binding_refused_command "printf '%s\n' 'Request target binding is invalid or ambiguous; no commit or push was attempted.' >&2; false"
  branch-excluded-patterns '["^(?:Do not|Never) (?:use|push to|commit to|work on) (?:the )?branch (.+)$"]'
  workflow-excluded-patterns '["^(?:Do not|Never) (?:save|write|create|place|put) (?:the |a )?(?:GitHub Actions )?workflow (?:as|at|to|in|under) ([^ ]+)"]'
  workflow-name-binding-patterns '["^(?:The |A )?(?:GitHub Actions |CI )?workflow (?:file )?(?:should|must) (?:have|use|be given) (?:a )?(?:meaningful |descriptive |clear )?(?:file ?)?name,? (?:like|such as|e\\.g\\.) ([^ ]+)$","^(?:Name|Call) (?:the |a )?(?:GitHub Actions |CI )?workflow (?:file )?(?:something )?(?:like|such as) ([^ ]+)$","^(?:Workflow|Рабочий процесс) (?:должен|должна) (?:иметь|называться) (?:осмысленное |понятное )?(?:имя|название)?,? (?:например|как) ([^ ]+)$"]'
  workflow-name-excluded-patterns '[]'
  workflow_path_file ".github/workflows/{file}"
  branch-forbidden-substrings '["..","@{"]'
  owned-clause-fence-prefixes '["~~~","```"]'

  task-scaffold-protocol-source "Hive Mind 8f22b87c515adece0427cb59e429531f35d7760a; official PR1254 .gitkeep blob 84fdaf2c70a1a770da99d0a3010884ebcad55ba8. Only the exact generated protocol with the current branch and request reference is removable; manual, modified, ambiguous and declared recipe files remain owned by their callers."
  task-scaffold-commit-command '(\nset -- {files}\nformal_ai_scaffold_declared=0\nfor formal_ai_path do\n  case "$formal_ai_path" in .gitkeep|./.gitkeep) formal_ai_scaffold_declared=1 ;; esac\ndone\nif [ "$formal_ai_scaffold_declared" -eq 0 ] && test -f .gitkeep && ! test -L .gitkeep &&\n  test -z "$(git rev-parse --show-prefix)" &&\n  git ls-files --error-unmatch -- .gitkeep >/dev/null 2>&1 &&\n  git diff --quiet -- .gitkeep && git diff --cached --quiet -- .gitkeep &&\n  formal_ai_scaffold_branch=$(git symbolic-ref --quiet --short HEAD) &&\n  LC_ALL=C awk -v "branch=$formal_ai_scaffold_branch" -v reference={reference} "NR != 1 { invalid = 1 }\nNR == 1 {\n  prefix = \"# .gitkeep file auto-generated at \"\n  suffix = \" for PR creation at branch \" branch \" for issue \" reference\n  timestamp = substr(\$0, length(prefix) + 1, 24)\n  if (length(\$0) != length(prefix) + 24 + length(suffix)) invalid = 1\n  if (substr(\$0, 1, length(prefix)) != prefix) invalid = 1\n  if (substr(\$0, length(prefix) + 25) != suffix) invalid = 1\n  if (timestamp !~ /^[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]T[0-9][0-9]:[0-9][0-9]:[0-9][0-9]\\.[0-9][0-9][0-9]Z\$/) invalid = 1\n  year = substr(timestamp, 1, 4) + 0\n  month = substr(timestamp, 6, 2) + 0\n  day = substr(timestamp, 9, 2) + 0\n  split(\"31 28 31 30 31 30 31 31 30 31 30 31\", days, \" \")\n  if (year % 4 == 0 && (year % 100 != 0 || year % 400 == 0)) days[2] = 29\n  if (month < 1 || month > 12 || day < 1 || day > days[month]) invalid = 1\n  if (substr(timestamp, 12, 2) + 0 > 23) invalid = 1\n  if (substr(timestamp, 15, 2) + 0 > 59) invalid = 1\n  if (substr(timestamp, 18, 2) + 0 > 59) invalid = 1\n}\nEND { exit (NR != 1 || invalid) }" .gitkeep; then\n  test -f .gitkeep && ! test -L .gitkeep && git diff --quiet -- .gitkeep &&\n    git diff --cached --quiet -- .gitkeep || exit $?\n  formal_ai_scaffold_head=$(git rev-parse HEAD) || exit $?\n  formal_ai_restore_scaffold(){\n    formal_ai_scaffold_status=$?\n    if [ "$formal_ai_scaffold_status" -ne 0 ] &&\n      [ "$(git rev-parse HEAD)" = "$formal_ai_scaffold_head" ] &&\n      ! test -e .gitkeep && ! test -L .gitkeep; then\n      git restore --source="$formal_ai_scaffold_head" --staged --worktree -- .gitkeep || exit $?\n    fi\n    exit "$formal_ai_scaffold_status"\n  }\n  trap formal_ai_restore_scaffold EXIT\n  rm -- .gitkeep || exit $?\n  set -- "$@" .gitkeep\nfi\n{retire}{commit}\n)'
  superseded-workflow-source "Issue #1162: the Kotlin and Scala deliveries of 2026-11 ended with run.yml from an earlier session and Main.yml from the resumed one, both generated for the same program. Only a tracked, unmodified, non-symlink workflow in the same directory that carries this generator's exact header line and name line for the same program is retired; every other workflow stays untouched."
  superseded-workflow-retire-command 'for formal_ai_workflow in {dir}/*.yml {dir}/*.yaml; do\n  test "$formal_ai_workflow" != {workflow} && test -f "$formal_ai_workflow" && ! test -L "$formal_ai_workflow" &&\n    git ls-files --error-unmatch -- "$formal_ai_workflow" >/dev/null 2>&1 &&\n    git diff --quiet -- "$formal_ai_workflow" && git diff --cached --quiet -- "$formal_ai_workflow" &&\n    grep -qxF -e {header} -- "$formal_ai_workflow" && grep -qxF -e {name} -- "$formal_ai_workflow" || continue\n  rm -- "$formal_ai_workflow" || exit $?\n  set -- "$@" "$formal_ai_workflow"\ndone\n'
  refspec-failure-markers '["src refspec","does not match any"]'
  git-push-command-pattern '\bgit\s+push\b'
  origin-push-command-pattern '\bgit\s+push\s+(?:(?:-q|--quiet)\s+)?origin\s+'

  pull-request-session-summary-pattern "^<!-- hive-mind:working-session-summary -->\n## Working session summary\n\n[\s\S]+\n\n---\n\*This summary was automatically extracted from the AI working session output\.\*$"
  pull-request-session-started-pattern "^🤖 \*\*AI Work Session Started\*\*\n\nStarted at [0-9TZ:.+-]+\. Please wait for it to finish before giving feedback\.\n\n_Runtime: solve `v[^`\n]+`(?: · [^`\n·]+ `[^`\n]+`)+_$"
  pull-request-solution-log-pattern "^## (?:🤖 Solution Draft Log|🚨 Solution Draft Failed|🔄 Auto-restart(?:-until-mergeable)? (?:Log )?[0-9]+/[0-9]+(?: Log)?|🔄 Auto-restart-until-mergeable Log \(iteration [0-9]+\)|📎 Intermediate working-session log \(killed session\))\n[\s\S]+\n\n---\n\*Now working session is ended, feel free to review and add any feedback on the solution draft\.\*$"
  pull-request-auto-restart-pattern "^## 🔄 Auto-restart (?:[0-9]+/[0-9]+|triggered \(iteration [0-9]+\))\n\n\*\*Reason:\*\* [^\n]+\n\nStarting new session to address the issues\.\n\n---\n\*Auto-restart-until-mergeable mode is active\.[^\n]*\*$"
  pull-request-restart-limit-pattern "^## ❌ Auto-restart [0-9]+/[0-9]+ - limit reached\n[\s\S]+\n\n(?:---\n\*This run is reported as failed because the auto-restart limit was reached\.\*|No more sessions will start automatically\. Resolve the blocker, or rerun with a higher `--auto-restart-max-iterations`\.)$"
  pull-request-ready-to-merge-pattern "^## ✅ Ready to merge\n\nThis pull request is now ready to be merged:(?:\n- [^\n]+)+(?:\n\n---\n\*Monitored by hive-mind with --auto-restart-until-mergeable flag\*)?$"
  pull-request-automation-stopped-pattern "^## 🛑 Automation stopped: [^\n]+\n[\s\S]+\n\n---\n\*Reported automatically by hive-mind \([a-z-]+\)\.\*$"
  pull-request-auto-restart-evidence-pattern "^## 🔄 Auto-restart [0-9]+/[0-9]+\n\n\*\*Reason:\*\* [^\n]+\n\n(?:\*\*Evidence:\*\*\n(?:- [^\n]+\n)+\n)?Starting a new session to address it\.$"
  pull-request-auto-restart-uncommitted-pattern "^## 🔄 Auto-restart [0-9]+/[0-9]+\n\n(?:Detected uncommitted changes from previous run\. Starting new session to review and commit or discard them\.|The previous session left uncommitted changes\. Starting a new session to commit or discard them\.)\n\n\*\*Uncommitted files:\*\*\n```\n[^`]*\n```(?:\n\n---\n\*Auto-restart will stop after changes are committed or discarded, or after [0-9]+ more iterations?\. Please wait until working session will end and give your feedback\.\*)?$"
  pull-request-restart-safety-limit-pattern "^## ⚠️ Auto-restart limit reached\n\nHive Mind stopped auto-restart-until-mergeable after [0-9]+ restart iterations\.\n[\s\S]+\n\n---\n\*Auto-restart-until-mergeable stopped by the safety limit\.\*$"
  pull-request-session-started-draft-pattern "^🤖 \*\*AI Work Session Started\*\*\n\nStarting automated work session at [0-9TZ:.+-]+\n\nThe PR has been converted to draft mode while work is in progress\.\n\n_This comment marks the beginning of an AI work session\. Please wait for the session to finish, and provide your feedback\._(?:\n\n_Runtime: solve `v[^`\n]+`(?: · [^`\n·]+ `[^`\n]+`)+_)?$"
  pull-request-solution-failed-pattern "^## 🚨 Solution Draft Failed\n[\s\S]+\n\nLogs were not attached because `--attach-logs` was not enabled, so this comment is the only surviving record of the failure\. Rerun with `--attach-logs --verbose` to publish the full session log with the raw tool error records\.$"
  pull-request-no-changes-pattern "^⚠️ \*\*No changes were produced by this session\*\*\n\nThe pull request (?:still )?has an empty diff against its base branch \(only the solver placeholder file is present\), so it (?:stays a draft instead of being|was not) marked ready for review\.(?:\n\nNothing was implemented, committed or pushed during this working session\. Review the session log above for why, then re-run the solver or continue manually\.| Check the session log for why, then rerun the solver or continue manually\.)$"
  pull-request-session-killed-pattern "^<!-- hive-mind:session-kill-notice -->\n## ❌ Working session was force-killed\n[\s\S]+\n\n<sub>Reported by Hive Mind</sub>$"
